          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fDz0gatyt_bKm4Gs7Bt--72" value="Launch Preparation" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1811" y="313" width="120" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fDz0gatyt_bKm4Gs7Bt--76" value="Here&#39;s a quick overview of your process:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. **Customer Interviews:** Gather insights from potential users to understand their needs and pain points.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. **Identify Problem:** Define and validate the problem you&#39;re aiming to solve.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. **Ideal Customer Profile:** Create a detailed profile of your target customer to guide development.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. **Requirements:** Define functional, non-functional, user, system, business, and regulatory requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;5. **Use Case:** Document scenarios that illustrate how users will interact with the software.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;6. **Visual Drawings and Diagrams:** Develop visual aids such as wireframes, mock-ups, user flows, schema designs, ERDs, class diagrams, and user story maps.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;7. **Development:** Build the software based on the defined requirements and designs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;8. **Release:** Progress through alpha, beta, release candidate, and stable release stages, gradually improving the product&#39;s polish and functionality.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;9. **Testing:** Conduct various types of testing to ensure the software&#39;s quality and performance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;10. **Launch Preparation:** Prepare the software, documentation, marketing materials, and support channels for launch.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;11. **Marketing &amp;amp; Launch:** Promote the software, generate interest, and officially release it to the market.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;12. **Sales:** Begin selling the software to customers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;13. **Improvements:** Continuously gather feedback, make improvements, and iterate on the software to enhance its value." style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1872" y="468" width="543" height="660" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fDz0gatyt_bKm4Gs7Bt--79" value="Improvements: Plan and Prioritize" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2211" y="313" width="120" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fDz0gatyt_bKm4Gs7Bt--84" value="Architecture Diagrams" style="shape=process;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1091" y="990" width="120" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fDz0gatyt_bKm4Gs7Bt--90" value="Based on the `package.json` file you provided, your app is using the following frameworks and libraries:&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;**Frameworks:**&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;1. **React:** A JavaScript library for building user interfaces.&#xa;   - `react`: The core library for building UI components.&#xa;   - `react-dom`: Used for rendering React components in the DOM.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;**UI Libraries:**&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;2. **Material-UI:** A popular React UI framework following Google&#39;s Material Design guidelines.&#xa;   - `@mui/icons-material`: Icons library for Material-UI.&#xa;   - `@mui/material`: Core Material-UI components and styles.&#xa;   - `@mui/styled-engine-sc`: Styling solution for Material-UI using styled-components.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;3. **PrimeReact:** A suite of rich UI components for React applications.&#xa;   - `primeicons`: Icons library for PrimeReact components.&#xa;   - `primereact`: PrimeReact UI components.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;**Styling Libraries:**&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;4. **Emotion:** A CSS-in-JS library for styling React components.&#xa;   - `@emotion/react`: Emotion library for styling.&#xa;   - `@emotion/styled`: Styled components with Emotion.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;5. **Styled-Components:** A popular CSS-in-JS library.&#xa;   - `styled-components`: Library for writing CSS within JavaScript using components.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;**Charting Library:**&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;6. **Recharts:** A charting library for creating interactive and customizable charts in React applications.&#xa;   - `recharts`: Library for creating charts.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;**Utility Libraries:**&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;7. **axios:** A promise-based HTTP client for making API requests.&#xa;   - `axios`: HTTP client library.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;8. **dayjs:** A library for working with dates and times.&#xa;   - `dayjs`: Date and time manipulation library.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;**Other Libraries:**&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;9. **Firebase:** A platform for building web and mobile applications.&#xa;   - `firebase`: Firebase services and features.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;10. **Miscellaneous:**&#xa;   - `@google-cloud/aiplatform`: Google Cloud&#39;s AI Platform APIs.&#xa;   - `@google-cloud/bigquery`: Google Cloud&#39;s BigQuery APIs.&#xa;   - `mui-calendar-picker`: A calendar picker component for Material-UI.&#xa;   - `emailjs-com`: Package for sending emails.&#xa;   - `web-vitals`: Package for measuring web performance metrics.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;The dependencies in your `package.json` file indicate that your app uses a combination of React, Material-UI, PrimeReact, Emotion, Styled-Components, Recharts, axios, dayjs, and various other packages. This suggests that your app likely focuses on building interactive user interfaces, data visualization, and potentially involves integrations with APIs and back-end services." style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2475" y="95" width="838" height="1061" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
